Formulas (simple, standard)
- CAC = (Sales & Marketing spend in period) / (Number of new customers acquired in period)
- ARPU (period) = (Revenue in period) / (Number of active customers in period)
- LTV (cohort-based, simplified) = ARPU_per_period * Gross_Margin% * Average_customer_lifetime_in_periods
  - Equivalent when using churn: LTV = (ARPU_per_period * Gross_Margin%) / Churn_rate_per_period
- CAC payback (months) = CAC / (ARPU_per_month * Gross_Margin%)
- Healthy rule-of-thumb targets: LTV : CAC >= 3x; CAC payback < 12 months (ideally 6–12 months for growth-stage).

